            <ArticleTitle>Migraine and cephalic cutaneous allodynia in pediatric patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1219-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Allodynia is a central sensitization state characterized by a perception of pain to normally nonpainful stimuli. The objective of this study was to determine the frequency of allodynia in children with migraine and to identify clinical features specific to this patient group.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
